---
import CaseStudy from './CaseStudy.astro';
---
<section id="work">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>Selected Work</h2>
      <p>A few projects from my time building software for biomedical R&D at BioMérieux. These projects show how I approach unfamiliar domains, collaborate with domain experts, and turn complex workflows into practical software.</p>
    </div>

    <CaseStudy
      title="Versioning System for Diagnostic Panel Development"
      sub="A web application for managing an iterative R&D workflow, developed in close collaboration with the scientists who used it."
      decisionTitle="Key Decision: Establish a shared vocabulary before encoding the workflow."
      color="var(--plum)"
    >
      <Fragment slot="problem">
        Diagnostic panel development was tracked in disparate spreadsheets across teams, with inconsistent formats and naming conventions. Hand-edited calculations could be unintentionally changed, and the resulting records did not clearly show how experiments and results evolved without additional context from the person who created them.
      </Fragment>
      <Fragment slot="role">
        <p>I co-designed the application with another team lead and worked directly with users to understand how they approached the work. A significant part of the requirements process was standardizing the vocabulary used to describe the workflow, helping establish shared terminology that could be reflected consistently in the application.</p>
        <p>I used user meetings, wireframes, and prototypes to work through the workflow and get feedback before committing to a final design. I then helped build and incrementally release the application, starting with versioning and tracking functionality and adding calculation support in a subsequent release.</p>
      </Fragment>
      <Fragment slot="decision">
        Different teams used different names and formats for related concepts. I led the effort to establish consistent terminology as part of requirements gathering, giving us a shared language for discussing the workflow and a more consistent foundation for the application.
      </Fragment>
      <Fragment slot="results">
        The resulting tool provided a more consistent way to track development and support calculations, while giving users a shared consistent workflow and terminology. Iterative releases let us validate the design with users and refine the application as we learned more about their needs.
      </Fragment>
    </CaseStudy>

    <!-- To add another project, copy the <CaseStudy> block above and change the
         props and slot text. Try color="var(--ochre)" or "var(--sage)". -->
  </div>
</section>
